            <h2 class="">
                TYPO3 Extensions
            </h2>

















        </header>







    <figure class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Extension-Key</th><th>Description / Comment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>paste_reference</td><td><p>The extension paste_reference is simplifying the work for editors in the backend. Even the project was not created by myself, I'm maintainer of the extension and care about all the upgrades and technical issues.</p><p>packagist: <a href="https://packagist.org/packages/ehaerer/paste-reference" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">packagist.org/packages/ehaerer/paste-reference</a></p></td></tr><tr><td>backend_theme_legacy</td><td><p>TYPO3 v14.3 got new icons in the backend. For accessibility reasons. I brought back the older icons with this extension.</p><p>packagist: <a href="https://packagist.org/packages/wdb/be-theme-legacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">packagist.org/packages/wdb/be-theme-legacy</a></p></td></tr><tr><td>theme_camino</td><td><p>I've created an appearance toggle (dark / light mode) for the theme camino, it didn't make it yet in the official version, and even it works fine a bit more work on the CSS would be good. On the linked website you also can change the theme color.</p><p>github: <a href="https://davidbruchmann.github.io/typo3-theme-camino/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">davidbruchmann.github.io/typo3-theme-camino</a></p></td></tr></tbody></table></figure><p>&nbsp;</p>














            </div>








            <div id="c18" class="frame frame-default frame-type-text frame-layout-0">













        <header>







            <h2 class="">
                Static Websites
            </h2>

















        </header>







    <figure class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Description / Comment</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://davidbruchmann.github.io/typo3-theme-camino/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">theme_camino (TYPO3)</a></td><td><p>Described above in TYPO3 extensions already, this a showcase for the theme camino with added feature. The rendered website is downloaded from the development server, so it could deployed as static website -- The source is nevertheless TYPO3.</p><p>TYPO3 is actually great for static websites, if no dynamic elements like forms are required. All benefits of TYPO3 can be used, and the site has to be saved statically, i.e. with httrack or just with wget or cUrl, then the website can be deployed. A good example is also this website, you're currently viewing!</p></td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://davidbruchmann.github.io/MiddleEast/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Middle East</a></td><td>The project “<a href="https://davidbruchmann.github.io/MiddleEast/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Middle East</a>” is a timeline about Israel in the Middle East and created without a framework, using a JavaScript-library for the timeline though. It's a start of work with an ongoing political process.<br>The project can certainly always be enriched with further data and is intended to be joined by a community for suggestions, opinions and further contributions.</td></tr><tr><td>backend_theme_legacy (Docusaurus)</td><td><p>The static website for the TYPO3 backend_theme_legacy was created with Docusaurus and is included in the code-repository.<br>It can be seen here: <a href="https://davidbruchmann.github.io/typo3-backend-theme-legacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">davidbruchmann.github.io/typo3-backend-theme-legacy</a><br><br>While there are several systems for static websites, Docusaurus is a great system to render mark-down files to static websites. It includes 3 different content categories by default:</p><ul><li data-list-item-id="ef1f1c9182902393cf22dc57f5d5fcbf4">docs: structured view with section-navigation for headlines, great for documentation.</li><li data-list-item-id="e5ae16a8db0aeb4e4ea60b6daf101bced">blog: blog with condense author-details above articles, great for individual articles, sorted primarily by date.</li><li data-list-item-id="eebcda13304c503b140efd82317430cf0">MJS/MJX elements for completely free design and structure, based on Require.js. This allows to create single pages or standardized page-types with own requirements.</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>














